{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.IsospinFromCanonicalBowtie","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.IsospinFromCanonicalBowtie","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.isospinFromCanonicalBowtie_refutable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.isospinFromCanonicalBowtie_refutable","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/isospin-from-canonical-bowtie.lean#L128-L139","doc":"The class is **refutable**, which the previous `holds : Prop` carrier was not: at\n`q = 2` the right-hand side is `(1/2)²·(3/2)·(5/2)·(1 + 1/8)/3 = 0.3515625`, so the\ninstance `⟨q := 2, ratio := 0⟩` cannot exist.\n\nThis is stated as a `theorem` rather than left implicit because \"the carrier asserts\nsomething\" is exactly the property that was missing, and a reader should be able to see it\ndischarged rather than take it on the docstring's word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IsospinFromCanonicalBowtie.residue_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IsospinFromCanonicalBowtie.residue_eq","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/isospin-from-canonical-bowtie.lean#L124-L124","doc":"**The content.** `Δm / M_N = ℏ_q² · h · [2]_q · (1 + ℏ_q³) / 3`, with\n`ℏ_q = 1 - q⁻¹`, `h = q - q⁻¹`, `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹` (symmetric). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IsospinFromCanonicalBowtie.q_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IsospinFromCanonicalBowtie.q_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/isospin-from-canonical-bowtie.lean#L121-L121","doc":"Away from the classical point `q = 1`, where the whole split degenerates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IsospinFromCanonicalBowtie.q_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IsospinFromCanonicalBowtie.q_pos","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/isospin-from-canonical-bowtie.lean#L119-L119","doc":"The substrate modulus is a genuine deformation parameter: positive and not the\nclassical point. Both are needed for `q⁻¹` to behave and for `h = q - q⁻¹` to be nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IsospinFromCanonicalBowtie.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IsospinFromCanonicalBowtie.mk","kind":"ctor","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/isospin-from-canonical-bowtie.lean#L116-L116","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IsospinFromCanonicalBowtie","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IsospinFromCanonicalBowtie","kind":"class","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/isospin-from-canonical-bowtie.lean#L104-L126","doc":"**CONJECTURE (D9).** Canonical `SU(2)_I` isospin from the operator-valued `⋈_K`\ninterface: the isospin-`ℤ/2`-antisymmetric residue of the regularised crystal functional\nresolves to the substrate flavour split.\n\n`q` is the substrate modulus and `ratio` the nucleon mass split `Δm / M_N`, both supplied\nby the caller — so the class is false at values that do not satisfy `residue_eq`, which is\nthe point (see the header). Factor conventions are the producer's, not the glyphs'.\n\n**No instance is provided.** Downstream results consume this as `[IsospinFromCanonicalBowtie q ratio]`\nand are genuinely conditional on it.\n\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] conj:isospin-from-canonical-bowtie ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:isospin-from-canonical-bowtie","label":"conj:isospin-from-canonical-bowtie","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/isospin-from-canonical-bowtie.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}